From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:08:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Give the cubic curves of CFF outlines as Windows
 gives them.

GetGlyphOutline took the cubic control points of a CFF outline for
quadratic ones: GGO_BEZIER turned each cubic curve into two, of six
points, and GGO_NATIVE gave the two control points as a quadratic
spline, neither of them the shape of the glyph.  Measured on Windows
with several CFF fonts from 16 to 4000 pixels: GGO_BEZIER gives each
cubic curve as it is, a record of three points; GGO_NATIVE gives it as
a record of n quadratic pieces, one if its third difference
p3 - 3 p2 + 3 p1 - p0 is at most a pixel in both directions, otherwise
the fewest, at least two, for which it is at most ten pixels times n
cubed.  The pieces cover equal ranges of the parameter, and each one's
control point is (3 (a1 + a2) - a0 - a3) / 4 of its cubic piece; this
matched all 1230 curves measured.  As their number depends on the size
on the device, the outline is transformed before its size is worked
out too.

A FIXED became an FT_Fixed through an unsigned int, which the 64-bit
unix side zero-extends, so any negative element of the matrix given to
GetGlyphOutline became about 65536: turned half round, a glyph's black
box was 52428000 pixels wide.

GGO_METRICS returns what Windows returns, the size of the glyph's
GLYPHBITS: 16 bytes of header and the black box as a bitmap with rows
of whole bytes, rounded up to four bytes, for every font quality and
also unhinted and transformed.

The test uses a small CFF font of its own; it passes on Windows, and
failed 40 times before.

